  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Higher Education and TVET Policies in the Arab region</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">With UNESCO Beirut as the secretariat, the Regional Convention on the Recognition of Studies, Diplomas, and Degrees in Higher Education in the Arab States is set to be in force upon the ratification by five countries. Functioning as a crucial tool, the Convention promotes student mobility and strengthens connections among higher education systems in the region. It advocates for the equitable, transparent, and non-discriminatory recognition of higher education qualifications, solidifying UNESCO Beirut&apos;s role in spearheading the Arab Higher Education Convention. This workplans aims to increase awareness and advocacy for the ratification of the Convention among Arab member states; coordinate and extend technical support and developing a ratification roadmap; strengthening the capacities of Arab member states to establish Higher Education centers; and initiate a policy dialogue on quality assurance in higher education institutions in specific countries.</narrative>
  </description>
